description:
Design a PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) signal generator with an adjustable duty cycle based on an 8-bit counter. The module takes a clock input (iClk) and a 4-bit wide pulse width value (iPWM). It uses an 8-bit counter to track the current count and outputs a PWM signal (oPWM) that is high for a duration determined by the iPWM input. When the counter reaches 100, it resets, and the output signal is set high if the current count is less than the specified pulse width value. Otherwise, the output is low. This module can be used to generate variable duty cycle PWM signals for controlling devices such as motors or LEDs.
module top_module(
	input iClk,
	input iPWM,
	output oPWM
);

