Design a circuit that calculates the parity bit for an n-bit wide input. The module takes an 8-bit input signal, computes the even parity by performing a bitwise XOR operation across all input bits, and outputs the resulting parity bit alongside the original input signals. When the parity bit is HIGH, it indicates that the number of HIGH input bits is even; when LOW, it indicates an odd number of HIGH input bits.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] in,
  output p,
  output [n-1:0] out
);

