Design a 4-bit binary to Gray code converter. The module takes a 4-bit binary input (B) and generates a corresponding 4-bit Gray code output (G). The conversion is achieved by XORing each bit of the binary input with a shifted version of itself, which helps ensure that only one bit changes at a time between successive values, as per the Gray code characteristics.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] B,
    output [3:0] G
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] B,
    output [3:0] G
);wire [3:0] shift_B;
    assign shift_B = {B[2:0], 1'b0};

    assign G[0] = B[0] ^ shift_B[0];
    assign G[1] = B[1] ^ shift_B[1];
    assign G[2] = B[2] ^ shift_B[2];
    assign G[3] = B[3] ^ shift_B[3];

endmodule

