description:
Design a circuit that implements a right-shifting operation on a 4-bit output based on a clock signal and a reset condition. The module uses a counter to track clock cycles, and upon reaching a specified threshold defined by the `count` input, it shifts the 4-bit `led_n` output to the right by one position. If `led_n` becomes zero, it resets it back to 8. The operation is synchronous to the clock and incorporates an active-low reset functionality, allowing for controlled shifting of the output.
module top_module(
    input clk, reset_n,
    input [31:0] count,
    output reg [3:0] led_n   
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk, reset_n,
    input [31:0] count,
    output reg [3:0] led_n   
);integer counter;

always @(posedge clk)begin
    if(!reset_n)begin
        counter = 0;
        led_n = 0;
    end

    counter = counter + 1;

    if(counter>=count)begin
        led_n = led_n >> 1;
        counter = 0;
    end

    led_n = (led_n==0) ? 8 : led_n;
end

endmodule

